@RPRX, I finished the cleanup and pushed the changes. I removed another 28 lines from VMess inbound. Ordinary TCP and UDP use the `DispatchLink` path from #5143. The remaining VMess code serializes concurrent replies before encryption, completes the response according to the protocol, and sends the VMess response header before Mux frames.

VMess outbound accepts `mux` in its original configuration location and uses the shared VLESS Multiplex implementation. I simplified Multiplex shutdown and Reverse, removed the long-running Reverse test, and kept the main Reverse scenario. I also fixed the TLS version check that broke Vision over mKCP.

All 11 protocol scenarios, interoperability checks with the earlier build, and targeted Multiplex tests with the race detector passed. The full PR is now 403 lines smaller than `main`.
